    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13489" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēsultōrĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		desultor. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to a
			vaulter</i> (desultor): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 39</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">levitas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 1, § 88</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">desultorius</span></b> , ii, m.,
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Mur. 27, 57</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Desultory, superficial</i>, Ap. M. 1, p. 102,
		14.</div>
